  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating HRDs safety and capacity for greater resilience and effective fulfilment of their mandates in Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DefendDefenders work focuses on  supporting HRDs at risk specifically, women HRDs, HRDs with disability and those working on disability rights, HRDs on environment and natural resources, and HRDs fighting impunity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program will contribute to enhanced safety and capacity of HRDs in the Uganda for greater resilience and effective fulfillment of their mandates.  Specifically, the project will contribute to three main objectives including: to enhance the availability, accessibility and utilization of emergency and medium-term protection services to HRDs at risk in Uganda; to strengthen policy influence and advocacy engagement at the national and international level for HRD safety; and to improve the capacity of individual HRDs to effectively do their work, respond and mitigate imminent risks and threats faced.The above objectives will contribute to the following outcomes: enhanced availability, accessibility, and utilisation of emergency and medium-term protection services to HRDs at risk; better policy reform and advocacy engagements with International and African human rights systems, national institution, and other relevant stakeholders for HRD safety; and strengthened organizational and technical capacity of individual HRDs, their organisations and national HRD coalition to effectively mitigate security risks and threats and continue their operations</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project contributes to DefendDefenders&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; protection and security management component which aims to increase the safety and security of HRDs, whether they face threats and imminent risk due to their human rights work or due to limited skills and knowledge in safety and security. Advocacy and policy influencing is derived as a main tool to address the legal and policy environment that is increasingly restricting HRDs and organisations supporting or executing HRD work. Capacity building is hinged on the realisation that the safety and continued operation of HRDs depends on the level of capacity/skills (capacity to do, capacity to be, and capacity to relate) resident within individual HRDs, their organisations, national coalitions, and the sub-regional networks.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a continuation from a project funded by the Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands for the protection and safety of HRDs in Uganda to contribute to a safe working for those HRDs from July 2018 to June 2021.</narrative>
  </description>
